# Cloudflare Pages security headers (D-49-38). This file lives at the flow-site PROJECT ROOT
# per the official adapter-cloudflare convention (RESEARCH A4 — NOT static/_headers; the
# adapter copies it into the build output, where static/_headers would be served as a literal
# asset and silently ignored).
#
# CSP rationale (T-49-01-HDR mitigation):
#   - script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' : the Phase 48 Mono-WASM runtime needs
#     wasm-unsafe-eval to instantiate its modules. Monaco is self-hosted (bundled via Vite,
#     RESEARCH Open Q1) so NO CDN allowance is required.
#   - connect-src 'self' + GitHub : gist creation (api.github.com) + OAuth (github.com) only.
#   - style-src 'unsafe-inline' : SvelteKit + Tailwind inject critical inline styles.
#   - script-src 'sha256-...' : the ONE inline early-theme script in app.html (D-49-20
#     FOUC-prevention — applies [data-theme] before first paint). Hashed, NOT 'unsafe-inline',
#     so the policy stays tight. If app.html's inline script body changes, recompute the hash:
#       node -e 'const fs=require("fs"),c=require("crypto");const b=fs.readFileSync("src/app.html","utf8").match(/<script>([\s\S]*?)<\/script>/)[1];console.log("sha256-"+c.createHash("sha256").update(b).digest("base64"))'
#
# COOP/COEP are SCOPED to /playground/* only (RESEARCH Open Q1) — the v1.6 AudioWorklet +
# SharedArrayBuffer foundation — so marketing/docs fonts + assets are unaffected. v1 WASM is
# single-threaded and needs no isolation; if these two lines cause subresource friction at
# Plan 49-05/08 they may be removed per HANDOFF §3 with no security loss. CSP + Permissions-Policy
# stay regardless.

/*
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(), camera=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-zDS2B0ul9twaEUuNWgi1IThSBeH5Sa0i56x2VNYO7Lg='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://github.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# NOTE: CF Pages globs do NOT match the bare path with `/*` alone — SvelteKit serves the
# playground document at exactly /playground (trailingSlash 'never'), and only the top-level
# DOCUMENT's COOP/COEP establish isolation. Both blocks are required (audit 2026-06-09 §6.8).
/playground
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/playground/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
